## 9. Result Typing for Complex Flows (Optional but Recommended)

- For pipelines with multiple failure modes, consider using a `Result` pattern with `dataclasses` to avoid exception-as-control-flow

```python
from dataclasses import dataclass
from typing import Generic, TypeVar

T = TypeVar("T")

@dataclass
class Success(Generic[T]):
    value: T

@dataclass
class Failure:
    error: GILError
    message: str

ProcessingResult = Success[bytes] | Failure
```

---

## 10. Enforcement Checklist

Before committing any Python file, verify:

- [ ] No bare `except:` or silent `pass` in except blocks
- [ ] All new exceptions inherit from the module base class
- [ ] All C++ binding calls are wrapped with domain exception translation
- [ ] Logging uses structured fields, not f-string messages alone
- [ ] All `from` chains preserved on re-raises
- [ ] No stack traces or internal paths exposed to UI layer
- [ ] I/O operations use `with` blocks and validate paths before opening
